From 4680f6abca1928d2d10786e5d9ba342c12444826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vdn-h100 <none@local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:39:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] vdn: never keep the DiT and the decoders on the card at
 once

At 768p on an 80 GiB card rank 0 dies twice over where ranks 1-7 are fine, and
both times the reason is the same: install_ulysses replicates the transformer on
every rank (45.2 GiB in fp8) but only the main rank carries the video and audio
VAEs, and those are ~11 GiB.

First in the denoising loop, where a block's activations want 10.33 GiB and
about 13 GiB is left:

  [rank0]: torch.OutOfMemoryError: Tried to allocate 10.33 GiB.
  GPU 0 has a total capacity of 79.18 GiB of which 8.69 GiB is free.
    File "src/models/ops/fused_block.py", line 106, in fast_block_forward

Then, once the decoders are deferred past the loop, in the decode itself, where
345 frames of 1344x768 want ~4 GiB more than remains:

  [rank0]: torch.OutOfMemoryError: Tried to allocate 3.98 GiB.
  GPU 0 has a total capacity of 79.18 GiB of which 3.92 GiB is free.
    File "src/inference/render.py", line 242, in decode_and_save

The two never need to be co-resident: the decoders are idle while denoising and
the transformer is idle while decoding. So the decoders are loaded after the loop
instead of before it, and the transformer is parked on the host before the
decode. Rank 0 then has the same headroom as every other rank at both moments.

Timed as their own `decoder_load_seconds` and `transformer_offload_seconds`
rather than folded into setup or decode, so the move is visible rather than
hidden. `denoise_seconds` -- the number upstream's published comparison is
measured on -- is untouched by both.

A 141 GiB H200 fits everything at once, which is why upstream loads decoders up
front and never offloads. src/inference/infer.py is single-GPU and unchanged.
